{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1001", "sample_idx": 28, "model_name": "mistralai/mistral-small-4-119b-2603", "content": "**A Most Excellent and Tragical Itinerary of a Journey to the Land of the Rising Sun**\n\n**Act I: Scene I** – **The Arrival in the Enchanted Isle**\n\nUpon the morrow’s dawn when golden Phoebus doth ascend\nThou shalt set foot in Nippon’s realm where ancient mysteries blend.\nAt Narita or Kansai fair where dragons guard the gate\nThy senses shall be ravished by the customs thou dost await.\n\n**Act I: Scene II** – **The Delights of Tokyo the Radiant**\n\nFirst to Tokyo thy steps shall turn a city vast and bright.\nWhere neon lights do dance upon the streets in endless night.\nVisit Shibuya’s scramble grand where throngs in haste do flow\nAnd Harajuku’s youth in fashions strange their curious fancies show.\n\nThe Imperial Palace where shoguns erstwhile held their sway\nAnd gardens fair where koi do glide in tranquil ballet.\nAkihabara’s wares of gleaming steel and wonders electronic\nShall tempt thy purse and fill thy mind with visions futuristic.\n\n**Act II: Scene I** – **The Journey to Mount Fuji’s Lofty Peak**\n\nA day’s travel to Hakone’s hot springs steaming in the air\nWhere ryokan’s gentle ministrations ease thy body’s care.\nMount Fuji’s snow-crowned majesty doth watch o’er land and sea\nA sight most wondrous and sublime for all eternity.\n\n**Act III: Scene I** – **Kyoto the Noble**\n\nTo Kyoto next thy path doth lead a city steeped in lore.\nWhere temples old and teahouses stand on streets of yore.\nFushimi Inari’s torii gates in vermilion rows ascend\nA path to gods where fox spirits their ancient secrets send.\n\nKinkaku-ji the Golden Pavilion gleams with light so bright\nReflected ‘pon the mirror pond a most celestial sight.\nArashiyama’s bamboo grove doth whisper in the breeze\nAnd Gion’s geisha in their grace do move with utmost ease.\n\n**Act IV: Scene I** – **The Haunted Forest and the Ancient Capital**\n\nTo Nara’s gentle deer who bow their heads in silent grace\nAnd Todai-ji’s great Buddha whose countenance doth embrace\nAll who with reverence draw nigh. The Kasuga Shrine’s stone path\nWhere lanterns hang in rows of old doth guard against the wrath\n\nOf time itself. Then to Osaka’s bustling merchant’s den\nWhere takoyaki’s savory scent doth rise and call to men.\nAnd Dotonbori’s garish lights do paint the night with hues\nMost vivid and most strange a feast for eyes and heart’s amuse.\n\n**Act V: Scene I** – **The Parting and the Promise of Return**\n\nWhen fourteen days have passed like dreams most sweet and all too brief\nThou shalt depart from Nippon’s shores upon the wings of grief.\nYet take with thee these memories bright of lands both old and new\nOf cherry blossoms soft and fleeting as the morning dew.\n\n**Epilogue: The Everlasting Memory**\n\nShouldst thou return to Nippon’s embrace as pilgrims oft do fare\nKnow that her charms shall ever call thee back with love’s sweet snare.\nFor in her isles of wonder where the sun doth rise anew\nThou hast found a second home beneath heavens strange and blue.", "logprobs": [{"token": "**", "logprob": -0.41663873195648193}, {"token": "A", "logprob": -0.04722839221358299}, {"token": " Most", "logprob": -0.9877652525901794}, {"token": " Excellent", "logprob": -1.9711520671844482}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.8003947734832764}, {"token": " Trag", "logprob": -1.201175570487976}, {"token": "ical", "logprob": -0.07170561701059341}, {"token": " It", "logprob": -0.005496152210980654}, {"token": "iner", "logprob": -0.00030179237364791334}, {"token": "ary", "logprob": -0.01210709847509861}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.637539803981781}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.4356432557106018}, {"token": " Journey", "logprob": -0.26315444707870483}, {"token": " to", "logprob": -0.23989686369895935}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.17326030135154724}, {"token": " Land", "logprob": -1.295870304107666}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.000284512090729549